   "label": "Table 1",
   "caption": "Peptide sequences and their characteristics.",
   "footnotes": [
    "a The calculated mass, pI value and net charge were obtained from Pepdraw (https://pepdraw.com/, accessed on 11 September 2023). b The observed mass was obtained by mass spectrum analysis by company (KR12 and CPP-KR12 from Genscript USA Inc. (Piscataway, NJ, USA) and CPP and FITC-CPP-KR12 from Peptron Inc. (Daejeon, Republic of Korea)). The N-terminus of each peptide was acetylated and the C-terminus was amidated. KR12 and CPP consist of residues 18 to 29 of the human cathelicidin LL-37 [25,26] and residues 49 to 57 (protein transduction domain) of the HIV TAT proteins [27,30], respectively. #: number of amino acid sequences; Ahx: 6-aminohexanoic acid; FITC: Fluorescein isothiocyanate."
